# 🔑 Step 2 — View the Source of the About Page

Navigate to the **About** page.

Right-click and select:

```text id="0ubq74"
View Page Source
```

Or press:

```text id="6a6b1g"
Ctrl + U
```

Search through the HTML source.

You should find something similar to:

```html id="rj2o3v"
<div notify_true="cGljb0NURnt3ZWJfc3VjYzNzc2Z1bGx5X2QzYzBkZWRfMDJjZGNiNTl9">
    ...
</div>
```

The suspicious part is:

```text id="g6d9x1"
notify_true="cGljb0NURnt3ZWJfc3VjYzNzc2Z1bGx5X2QzYzBkZWRfMDJjZGNiNTl9"
```

The `notify_true` attribute is a custom HTML attribute containing a Base64-encoded string.

> 🚨 **Key observation:** When doing web CTFs, unusual HTML attributes and long encoded strings are worth investigating.

